NAME
  bundle - pack files into one bundle and unpack it on another computer

SYNOPSIS
  bundle pack DIR [--out=FILE] [--raw] [--sfx]
  bundle pack FILE PATH... [--root=DIR] [--raw] [--sfx]
  bundle unpack FILE [--root=DIR]
  bundle list FILE

DESCRIPTION
  pack DIR packs a project folder as its bundle.cfg describes, a serialized table:
    {name="mill", paths={"etc","usr"}, exclude={"usr/lib/lz4.lua"}}
  name defaults to the folder name; the bundle is written beside the folder as NAME.bundle.
  pack FILE PATH... packs each PATH relative to --root (default: the working directory).
  unpack writes every file under --root (default: /). list prints the files in a bundle.

OPTIONS
  --out=FILE
    Write the bundle of a project folder to FILE.

  --raw
    Write an uncompressed bundle. Bundles are LZ4-compressed by default.

  --sfx
    Write a raw bundle with a small unpacker in front, as NAME.lua. Run it on a computer that
    has nothing installed: NAME.lua [--root=DIR].

  --root=DIR
    The folder paths are packed from or unpacked into.
